// Copy this file to Secrets.xcconfig (gitignored) and fill in your endpoint.
// Secrets.xcconfig is the project's base configuration for Debug and Release, so
// COSMOS_ENDPOINT gets substituted into Info.plist at build time. On Xcode Cloud,
// ci_scripts/ci_post_clone.sh writes this file from the workflow's COSMOS_ENDPOINT
// environment variable.
//
// The Cosmos primary key does NOT go here. Anything substituted into Info.plist
// ships readable inside the .ipa, so the key is pasted into the app once on first
// launch (CosmosKeyEntryView) and kept in Keychain.
//
// xcconfig gotchas, both found the hard way:
//
// 1. A literal `//` ANYWHERE in a line starts a comment and truncates the rest of
//    the line, with no error. This is why COSMOS_ENDPOINT below is built from a
//    $(SLASH) variable instead of written with "https://" directly.
//
// 2. Wrapping a value in quotes does NOT protect against #1, and when a quoted
//    value is substituted into an Info.plist string the literal quote characters
//    end up IN the string. So: no quotes around values, ever.
SLASH = /

COSMOS_ENDPOINT = https:$(SLASH)$(SLASH)your-account.documents.azure.com:443$(SLASH)
